    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"224323\">@Junyan Xu</span> ,  The following Lean 4 file <code>problem.lean</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">expose</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">native_decide</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>checks in <code>lake build</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">build</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">problem</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Build</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">completed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">successfully</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">jobs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The same file run through <code>con-ron --verified</code> gets rejected, because <code>native_decide</code> introduces an axiom:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">./</span><span class=\"n\">lean4export</span><span class=\"bp\">/.</span><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">build</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">bin</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">lean4export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">problem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">problem</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ndjson</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">con</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">ron</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--verified problem.ndjson</span>\n<span class=\"n\">con</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">ron</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">blocks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">modelled</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">process</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">30</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">generated</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">records</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checked</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">declarations</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">counted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">records</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">con</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">ron</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">declined</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">non</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">standard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">axiom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">axiom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">private</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">problem</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">0</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">native</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">native_decide</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ax_1_1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">position</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">46993</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"c1\">--verified) t=3.351s</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here is a Lean 4 file <code>workaround.lean</code> which avoids <code>native_decide</code> in favor of <code>decide</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">expose</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">section</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">decide</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">kernel</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This passes both <code>lake build</code> and <code>con-ron</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">build</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">workaround</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Build</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">completed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">successfully</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">jobs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">./</span><span class=\"n\">lean4export</span><span class=\"bp\">/.</span><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">build</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">bin</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">lean4export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">workaround</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">tmp</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">workaround</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ndjson</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">home</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">catskills</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">con</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">ron</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">release</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">con</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">ron</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--verified /tmp/workaround.ndjson</span>\n<span class=\"n\">con</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">ron</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">blocks</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">modelled</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">process</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">30</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">generated</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">records</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">checked</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">declarations</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">counted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">records</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">con</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">ron</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">accepted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">57921</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">declarations</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"c1\">--verified)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The following run uses <code>native_decide</code>.  It is in the queue and is in failed status with advice \"This is a fault at our end, not with your submission\" and \"Palomar must fix this. Do not change the repository. Palomar must examine this run; report the workflow URL.\"  It has been in the queue for 6 days.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Repository</span>\n<span class=\"n\">catskillsresearch</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">qlambda</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Commit</span>\n<span class=\"n\">c445d4610c3ce9137933e6e93f084ffb6d51c91b</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Comparator</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">configuration</span>\n<span class=\"n\">comparator</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">json</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Submitted</span>\n<span class=\"mi\">2026</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">09</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">28</span><span class=\"n\">T07</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">22</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">49</span><span class=\"n\">Z</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Verification</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span>\n<span class=\"mi\">36391338184</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"904x794\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/jUb5xV5amrL_uRKKH8I4E6Hk/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/jUb5xV5amrL_uRKKH8I4E6Hk/image.png/840x560.webp\"></p>\n<p>Should I:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Wait for you to change con-ron to accept <code>native_decide</code> with <code>--verified</code>.</li>\n<li>Change the repository to replace <code>native_decide</code> with <code>decide</code>, withdraw the run and resubmit it</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 629093193,
        "sender_full_name": "Lars Ericson",
        "timestamp": 1791158097
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not a developer of con-ron and certainly don't know enough about its code to \"change\" it.<br>\nRejecting <code>native_decide</code> seems to be the intended behavior, see <a href=\"https://palomar-registry.org/how-to-submit#extra-axioms\">https://palomar-registry.org/how-to-submit#extra-axioms</a>. So the question is why the official Lean kernel accepted it. Given this, I suggest you replace <code>native_decide</code> with <code>decide</code>, withdraw the run and resubmit it.</p>",
        "id": 629122002,
        "sender_full_name": "Junyan Xu",
        "timestamp": 1791172819
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><strong>Palomer maintainers</strong>, please opine.  I may get a submission rate penalty if I withdraw and submit a new version.  This seems to be an issue where mechanical verification should treat <code>native_decide</code> as not suitable for Palomar, similar to <code>sorry</code>, <code>axiom</code> and <code>admit</code>, prior to reaching <code>con-ron</code>.  Alternatively, <code>con-ron</code> could be patched to treat occurrences of <code>native_decide</code> as <code>decide +kernel</code>, which it allows.</p>",
        "id": 629180497,
        "sender_full_name": "Lars Ericson",
        "timestamp": 1791192065
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The thing is: <code>native_decide</code> is not fully equivalent to <code>decide +kernel</code> (for instance, the latter may time out when the former doesn't), so this is not a replacement Palomar could make. You should fix your repository.</p>",
        "id": 629181375,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1791192311
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree the Palomar error message is misleading here; this one is actually your code being non-compliant. Palomar's documentation is very clear to me.<br>\nCC <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110087\">@Kim Morrison</span> just so you see this</p>\n<p>(I'm not part of Palomar governance/admin at all, but as mathlib maintainer I feel confident about the technical assessment here.)</p>",
        "id": 629181674,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1791192385
    }
]